WEBVTT

00:00:07.131 --> 00:00:08.557
<v><b>Dave:</b></v> Have you finished packing?

00:00:09.107 --> 00:00:10.810
The taxi will be here in 15 minutes.

00:00:11.270 --> 00:00:12.757
<v><b>Becca:</b></v> Er, nearly.

00:00:13.043 --> 00:00:14.484
I can’t decide what to take.

00:00:14.526 --> 00:00:15.379
<v><b>Dave:</b></v> Well hurry up.

00:00:17.676 --> 00:00:19.156
You don’t need all that!

00:00:19.447 --> 00:00:21.120
You’ll never close that suitcase.

00:00:21.559 --> 00:00:23.435
And we can only take 20 kilos each.

00:00:23.436 --> 00:00:24.545
<v><b>Becca:</b></v> Yes, I know.

00:00:25.872 --> 00:00:27.295
<v><b>Dave:</b></v> You don’t need your trainers.

00:00:27.772 --> 00:00:29.402
We’ll be on the beach most of the time!

00:00:29.433 --> 00:00:31.466
<v><b>Becca:</b></v> What…I might go to the gym.

00:00:31.966 --> 00:00:33.088
There’s one in the hotel.

00:00:34.267 --> 00:00:35.876
<v><b>Dave:</b></v> And why are you taking a raincoat?

00:00:35.877 --> 00:00:38.088
It’s not going to rain in Greece in June.

00:00:38.104 --> 00:00:39.279
<v><b>Becca:</b></v> It might rain.

00:00:39.280 --> 00:00:41.091
It sometimes rains in the summer.

00:00:41.587 --> 00:00:42.372
<v><b>Dave:</b></v> And what’s that?

00:00:43.066 --> 00:00:44.173
<v><b>Becca:</b></v> That’s my hairdryer.

00:00:44.559 --> 00:00:46.595
<v><b>Dave:</b></v> But the hotel will have a hairdryer.

00:00:47.193 --> 00:00:48.432
<v><b>Becca:</b></v> It might not have one.

00:00:48.433 --> 00:00:50.566
Not all hotels have hairdryers.

00:00:50.750 --> 00:00:51.603
And I need it.

00:00:51.950 --> 00:00:53.986
<v><b>Dave:</b></v> And three pairs of jeans?

00:00:54.381 --> 00:00:56.113
We’re only going to be there for a week.

00:00:56.198 --> 00:00:57.882
<v><b>Becca:</b></v> They’re all different styles.

00:00:58.125 --> 00:00:59.916
I’m not sure which one I’ll want to wear.

00:01:00.896 --> 00:01:02.726
<v><b>Dave:</b></v> You need to take some things out.

00:01:02.727 --> 00:01:04.399
Extra baggage costs a fortune.

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:06.802
It’s something like 10 pounds per kilo.

00:01:06.971 --> 00:01:08.690
<v><b>Becca:</b></v> No, no, it’ll be fine, I promise.

00:01:13.072 --> 00:01:14.055
<v><b>Dave:</b></v> Hurry up.

00:01:14.330 --> 00:01:16.163
The traffic might be bad because of the rain.

00:01:16.576 --> 00:01:19.169
<v><b>Becca:</b></v> OK, I’ll be ready in…five minutes.

00:01:30.975 --> 00:01:31.987
<v><b>Dave:</b></v> The taxi’s here.

00:01:32.552 --> 00:01:33.951
<v><b>Becca:</b></v> OK, I’m ready.

00:01:34.258 --> 00:01:36.472
Can you take my case downstairs?

00:01:40.628 --> 00:01:42.762
<v><b>Dave:</b></v> Erg, I’m sure this is more than 20 kilos.

00:01:43.249 --> 00:01:44.863
It’s definitely heavier than my case.

00:01:46.147 --> 00:01:48.214
<v><b>Becca:</b></v> I’m sure it’ll be OK…